     "body": "<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3Abfcf2b10-5443-4304-afe6-3aff38ddf271\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"557058:bfcf2b10-5443-4304-afe6-3aff38ddf271\" data-account-id=\"557058:bfcf2b10-5443-4304-afe6-3aff38ddf271\" accountid=\"557058:bfcf2b10-5443-4304-afe6-3aff38ddf271\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Joshua Allan Westgard</a>, <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" data-account-id=\"60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" accountid=\"60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Danny Bernstein</a>: All of the bag files are in the top directory and the data directory is just like the export directory, so, for export, I think you'd just need to add:<br/>\nbagit.py --validate /path/to/export<br/>\nverify.py /path/to/export/data<br/>\n(I'm assuming verify.py already handles a -r that is not the base URL, as well as user-supplied predicates. bagit.py would also need to be added to the requirements. Import might be more complicated ...)</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/LibraryOfCongress/bagit-python\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/LibraryOfCongress/bagit-python</a></p>",
